      "description": "Identifies tables where sequential scans are performed more significantly than index scans, suggesting missing or inefficient indexes.\nThese tables meet the following conditions:\n\t•\tseq_scan > 100 — frequently scanned sequentially\n\t•\tidx_scan < seq_scan — index usage is low compared to seq scans\n\t•\tA high seq_to_idx_ratio indicates potential optimization opportunities\n\nIf no such tables are found, a placeholder row is returned.\n\nThis view helps detect tables that may benefit from new indexes to improve query performance",
